  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\mathrm{A}=\\{\\theta: \\sin (\\theta)=\\tan (\\theta)\\}$ and $\\mathrm{B}=(\\theta: \\cos (\\theta)=$ 1\\} be two sets. Then:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "bfcFu",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{A}=\\mathrm{B}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "42dDB",
      "text": "\n$A \\not \\subset B$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "vulSV",
      "text": "\n$B \\not \\subset A$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "tG3WW",
      "text": "\n$A \\subset B$ and $B-A \\neq \\phi$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $\\mathrm{A}=\\{\\theta: \\sin \\theta=\\tan \\theta\\}$ and $\\mathrm{B}=\\{\\theta: \\cos \\theta=1\\}$\nNow, $A=\\left\\{\\theta: \\sin \\theta=\\frac{\\sin \\theta}{\\cos \\theta}\\right\\}$ $=\\{\\theta: \\sin \\theta(\\cos \\theta-1)=0\\}$ $=\\{\\theta=0, \\pi, 2 \\pi, 3 \\pi, \\ldots \\ldots\\}$\nFor $\\mathrm{B}: \\cos \\theta=1 \\Rightarrow \\theta=\\pi, 2 \\pi, 4 \\pi, \\ldots \\ldots$\nThis shows that $\\mathrm{A}$ is not contained in B. i.e. $\\mathrm{A} \\not \\subset \\mathrm{B}$. but $\\mathrm{B} \\subset \\mathrm{A}$.",
    "image": null
  },
